{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788197997,"nonce":"a7se9461sPjZ1YSDfePaIKjGjLw=","message":"CLOSED — audited, fixed, merged and verified in-game on BORGES.\nMerged `5074a5b`; audit fixes `addd6d3`; DLL `09a4ace`.\n\n\nThe auditor decompiled the bench copy of `FindSuitableWeaponAndAmmo.dll` with\n`ilspycmd` (only the binary is on BORGES) rather than trusting the issue text.\n**The diagnosis survived, including all three of the worker's self-corrections.**\nVerified by member: `AutoArmTracker.IsAutoArm/SetAutoArm/Get`;\n`PawnColumnWorker_AutoArm.HasCheckbox` = `IsColonist \u0026\u0026 !WorkTagIsDisabled(Violent)`;\n`Patch_PawnGizmos.Postfix`'s second route; `MpSync.Configurable`;\n`FSWA_MapComponent.CollectCandidates` excluding forbidden and burning things.\n\n\n1. **A fabricated `false` that no `catch` could see.** `IsAutoArm` is\n   `Get?.optedIn.Contains(pawn) ?? false`, so a missing `AutoArmTracker` answers\n   the LEGAL value `false` and never throws. The write path caught it by\n   read-back; the observer did not, and would have published \"auto-arm is off\"\n   for a game whose tracker was gone. It also made `auto_arm:false` report\n   `applied` over a no-op.\n2. **Two OPTIONAL probes sat inside a `catch` that nulls the lever** — both\n   commented as costing \"the explanation, not the lever\". A throw in either\n   would have disabled a lever whose core members had already bound.\n\n\n3. The claim that a colonist's own drop lands UNFORBIDDEN was **backwards**.\n   `Verse/Pawn_EquipmentTracker.TryDropEquipment(eq, out eq, pos, bool forbid = true)`\n   calls `SetForbidden(forbid)`, and `RimWorld/JobDriver_DropEquipment` passes\n   three arguments — so the default applies and the drop lands FORBIDDEN.\n   `CollectCandidates` excludes forbidden things, so phase 4 would have failed as\n   \"no candidate weapons\" and read as a broken lever. **Phase 4.5's `unforbid` is\n   load-bearing, not belt-and-braces.** Independently re-verified by the\n   orchestrator against the decompiled member before merge.\n4. The phase-4 fixture table was wrong by omission — `CollectEligiblePawns` also\n   requires Spawned, on-map, `!Downed`, no mental state, not caravan-packing,\n   **not Drafted**, no equip job in flight, and Manipulation. Each silently drops\n   the pawn while `auto_arm` still reads `true`.\n\n\n    1.1  pawn {sections:[\"area\"]}  -\u003e auto_arm: false (a real Boolean),\n                                      no auto_arm_unknown\n    1.2  assign {med_care:\"Best\"}  -\u003e levers:[], no auto_arm_mod key —\n                                      a call without the lever does not touch it\n    2.1  assign {auto_arm:true}    -\u003e accepted:1, applied:[\"auto_arm\"],\n                                      before:false -\u003e after:true,\n                                      action.journal_seq: 54\n         auto_arm_mod: {loaded:true, tracker:true, mech_route:true}\n    2.2  pawn {sections:[\"area\"]}  -\u003e auto_arm: true   (observer agrees)\n    2.4  assign {auto_arm:false}   -\u003e before:true -\u003e after:false\n    2.7  journal {types:[\"warning\"]} -\u003e 0 warnings, 0 FSWA-related\n\n`2.7` is the one that matters most: the bridge reads back from FSWA's own tracker\nafter every write, so before/after agreeing with an independent observer read,\nwith zero bridge warnings, is evidence the reflection reached the real mod rather\nthan a field we own.\n\n**The gate was also proved on the refusal path, unplanned.** All three colonists\non the fixture are incapable of Violence, so the first flip was REFUSED with both\nwidgets cited verbatim: *\"this pawn is incapable of Violence: the Assign-tab\ncheckbox is not drawn (PawnColumnWorker_AutoArm.HasCheckbox) and the gizmo is\ndisabled with FSWA_CannotViolent\"*. The accept path then needed a staged pawn —\n`dev:spawn-pawn {violence_capable:true}`.\n\n**FIXTURE GAP FOR THE NEXT RUN: `autostart.rws` has NO violence-capable\ncolonist.** Not in any fixture table. Stage one, or the accept path cannot run.\n\nZero red errors across the entire bench session.\n\n\n- **The absent-mod path.** Needs a `ModsConfig.xml` edit and a restart; not run.\n  `auto_arm_mod.loaded:false` and the `null`-not-`false` contract are unproven\n  at runtime.\n- **The API-drift path**, reachable only by editing FSWA.\n- **The weapon-capable-mechanoid branch** — needs Fortified Framework / DMS and a\n  pawn implementing `Fortified.IWeaponUsable`; unreachable on this bench.\n- **The arming pass itself.** I proved the LEVER, not the BEHAVIOUR: no run\n  showed a pawn actually walking to a weapon and equipping it under `advance`\n  with no `equip` order. That is phases 4.3-4.9 of `accept/auto-arm-lever.md`\n  and it was not executed.\n- **Multiplayer.** `MpSync` registration was read, never exercised.\n- There is still **no `.ps1` driver** for `accept/auto-arm-lever.md`; the above\n  was hand-driven as raw file protocol.","files":null}]}